WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.455
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Grammar, level B one.

2
00:00:05.755 --> 00:00:09.489
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.789 --> 00:00:15.867
Unit five: Passive Voice (basic). Today you will focus on the action rather than the person who did it.

4
00:00:16.167 --> 00:00:18.842
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:19.800 --> 00:00:22.743
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:23.583 --> 00:00:24.596
Is made.

7
00:00:25.583 --> 00:00:27.873
Is made means the present passive of make.

8
00:00:28.483 --> 00:00:29.798
Rice is made here.

9
00:00:30.383 --> 00:00:32.687
Your turn. Say: Is made.

10
00:00:35.533 --> 00:00:36.465
Is made.

11
00:00:37.217 --> 00:00:38.090
Was built.

12
00:00:39.083 --> 00:00:41.501
Was built means the past passive of build.

13
00:00:42.117 --> 00:00:43.942
The temple was built long ago.

14
00:00:44.550 --> 00:00:46.633
Your turn. Say: Was built.

15
00:00:49.500 --> 00:00:50.478
Was built.

16
00:00:51.217 --> 00:00:51.997
By.

17
00:00:52.983 --> 00:00:56.248
By means introduces the agent in a passive sentence.

18
00:00:56.850 --> 00:00:58.420
The song was written by her.

19
00:00:59.017 --> 00:01:01.205
Your turn. Say: By.

20
00:01:04.067 --> 00:01:04.928
By.

21
00:01:05.683 --> 00:01:06.963
Active voice.

22
00:01:07.950 --> 00:01:11.180
Active voice means a sentence where the subject does the action.

23
00:01:11.783 --> 00:01:13.226
The chef cooked the meal.

24
00:01:13.817 --> 00:01:16.539
Your turn. Say: Active voice.

25
00:01:19.400 --> 00:01:20.622
Active voice.

26
00:01:21.383 --> 00:01:22.768
Passive voice.

27
00:01:23.783 --> 00:01:27.292
Passive voice means a sentence where the subject receives the action.

28
00:01:27.883 --> 00:01:29.558
The meal was cooked by the chef.

29
00:01:30.150 --> 00:01:32.744
Your turn. Say: Passive voice.

30
00:01:35.600 --> 00:01:36.752
Passive voice.

31
00:01:37.517 --> 00:01:38.413
Subject.

32
00:01:39.417 --> 00:01:42.415
Subject means the person or thing the sentence is about.

33
00:01:43.017 --> 00:01:44.563
The chef is the subject.

34
00:01:45.150 --> 00:01:47.466
Your turn. Say: Subject.

35
00:01:50.300 --> 00:01:51.289
Subject.

36
00:01:52.050 --> 00:01:52.970
Object.

37
00:01:53.983 --> 00:01:56.877
Object means the person or thing that receives the action.

38
00:01:57.483 --> 00:01:58.844
The meal is the object.

39
00:01:59.450 --> 00:02:02.137
Your turn. Say: Object.

40
00:02:05.000 --> 00:02:05.873
Object.

41
00:02:06.617 --> 00:02:07.595
Focus.

42
00:02:08.583 --> 00:02:11.477
Focus means the main thing that we want to talk about.

43
00:02:12.083 --> 00:02:13.688
The focus is on the meal.

44
00:02:14.283 --> 00:02:16.494
Your turn. Say: Focus.

45
00:02:19.333 --> 00:02:20.276
Focus.

46
00:02:21.067 --> 00:02:24.520
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:25.383 --> 00:02:29.324
Visal, change this to the passive: 'The chef cooked the meal.'

48
00:02:30.417 --> 00:02:41.277
The meal was cooked by the chef. In the passive, the object of the active sentence becomes the subject, and the verb is be + past participle.

49
00:02:42.383 --> 00:02:43.779
Why use the passive?

50
00:02:44.883 --> 00:02:55.941
When the action or result is more important than the person, or when we do not know the person: The window was broken. Newspapers and reports use it often.

51
00:02:57.050 --> 00:02:58.515
When do we use by?

52
00:02:59.617 --> 00:03:13.673
Only if the agent is important or surprising: The song was written by a famous singer. If it is not important, we leave it out. The tense is shown by the verb be: is made, was made.

53
00:03:14.833 --> 00:03:16.624
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:17.483 --> 00:03:21.689
Grammar focus: Passive voice: be plus past participle.

55
00:03:21.989 --> 00:03:23.141
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:23.850 --> 00:03:25.652
The meal was cooked by the chef.

57
00:03:26.550 --> 00:03:28.457
Rice is grown in Cambodia.

58
00:03:29.350 --> 00:03:31.338
The window was broken last night.

59
00:03:32.300 --> 00:03:40.563
Passive = be + past participle. The object of the active sentence becomes the subject. Add by + agent only if it matters.

60
00:03:41.317 --> 00:03:44.921
Be careful! Don't say: The letter was wrote yesterday.

61
00:03:46.867 --> 00:03:49.540
Say: The letter was written yesterday.

62
00:03:49.840 --> 00:03:51.537
Use the past participle.

63
00:03:52.333 --> 00:03:55.032
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:55.833 --> 00:03:56.765
Who Did It?.

65
00:03:57.065 --> 00:03:59.761
In the active voice, the chef cooked the meal.

66
00:04:00.767 --> 00:04:04.090
In the passive voice, the meal was cooked by the chef.

67
00:04:05.100 --> 00:04:07.785
Rice is grown in many parts of Cambodia.

68
00:04:08.800 --> 00:04:11.218
This temple was built a long time ago.

69
00:04:12.233 --> 00:04:15.835
The focus of a passive sentence is the action, not the person.

70
00:04:16.933 --> 00:04:21.179
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:22.017 --> 00:04:23.668
The cake blank by my mother.

72
00:04:23.968 --> 00:04:27.482
A, made. B, was made. C, is make.

73
00:04:31.033 --> 00:04:33.126
The answer is B: was made.

74
00:04:34.283 --> 00:04:36.144
Rice blank in Cambodia.

75
00:04:36.444 --> 00:04:39.876
A, is grown. B, grows by. C, grown.

76
00:04:43.433 --> 00:04:45.653
The answer is A: is grown.

77
00:04:46.817 --> 00:04:49.919
In a passive sentence, the blank becomes the subject.

78
00:04:50.219 --> 00:04:53.246
A, object. B, agent. C, verb.

79
00:04:56.800 --> 00:04:59.009
The answer is A: object.

80
00:05:00.150 --> 00:05:01.801
Which sentence is correct?

81
00:05:02.101 --> 00:05:06.904
A, The letter was wrote.. B, The letter was written.. C, The letter written was..

82
00:05:10.467 --> 00:05:12.861
The answer is B: The letter was written..

83
00:05:14.017 --> 00:05:17.943
According to the reading, what is the focus of a passive sentence?

84
00:05:18.243 --> 00:05:22.187
A, the action. B, the cook. C, the weather.

85
00:05:25.733 --> 00:05:27.791
The answer is A: the action.

86
00:05:29.000 --> 00:05:31.838
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:32.683 --> 00:05:36.090
Change this to passive: 'The chef cooked the meal.'

88
00:05:44.883 --> 00:05:46.291
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:05:46.591 --> 00:06:00.089
The meal was cooked by the chef. In this sentence, the meal becomes the subject, and I use was cooked, which is be + past participle. The chef appears after by because it is important information.

90
00:06:00.389 --> 00:06:02.226
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:06:03.117 --> 00:06:08.811
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and passive voice: be plus past participle.

92
00:06:09.111 --> 00:06:12.959
Today's value is precision. Choose your words and numbers with care.

93
00:06:13.259 --> 00:06:15.865
See you in Unit six. Goodbye!

94
00:06:16.165 --> 00:06:18.875
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

